<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformation Replacement with Environment Variables and AWS SSM Parameter Store
  ============================================================================================================
  This Web.Debug.config transformation file has been DEPRECATED as part of the cloud readiness migration.

  REASON: Web.config build-time transformations (Web.Debug.config, Web.Release.config) are incompatible
  with cloud deployment pipelines where configuration must be externalized and runtime-configurable.
  Build-time transformations bake environment-specific values into deployment artifacts, preventing
  immutable deployments and true infrastructure-as-code on AWS.

  REPLACEMENT: All environment-specific configuration is now injected at runtime via:

  1. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (highest priority)
     Set the following environment variables in your AWS deployment target:
     - ECS Task Definition: add environment variables in the container definition
     - Elastic Beanstalk: set in Configuration > Software > Environment Properties
     - EC2 / on-premises: set in the OS environment or systemd unit file

     Required environment variables:
       RDS_CONNECTION_STRING   — Full ADO.NET connection string to the Amazon RDS instance or RDS Proxy endpoint
                                 Example: Server=mydb.cluster-xxxx.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com;Database=tourdb;
                                          User Id=admin;Password=<from-secrets-manager>;

       SSM_DBCONNECTION        — Alternative: inject the connection string from AWS SSM Parameter Store.
                                 Configure your ECS task definition or Elastic Beanstalk environment to
                                 resolve the SSM parameter /tour-management/dbconnection and inject its
                                 value as this environment variable.

       AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME      — Name of the S3 bucket used for tour image uploads (cr-dotnet-1032)
       AWS_REGION              — AWS region for SDK clients (e.g. us-east-1)

  2. AWS SYSTEMS MANAGER PARAMETER STORE
     Store sensitive configuration values as SecureString parameters:
       /tour-management/dbconnection   — RDS connection string (SecureString)
       /tour-management/s3-bucket      — S3 bucket name (String)

     Reference these parameters in your ECS task definition using the "secrets" field:
       {
         "name": "SSM_DBCONNECTION",
         "valueFrom": "arn:aws:ssm:us-east-1:ACCOUNT_ID:parameter/tour-management/dbconnection"
       }

  3. AWS SECRETS MANAGER (recommended for credentials)
     Store database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and reference them in the ECS task definition
     or inject them into the connection string at application startup.

  NOTE: This file is intentionally left as a no-op stub. Do NOT add XDT transformation directives here.
  All configuration management is handled at runtime via environment variables and AWS SSM Parameter Store.
-->

<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No XDT transformations are applied in this file.
    Configuration is managed at runtime via environment variables and AWS SSM Parameter Store.
    See the comments above for the full migration guide.
  -->
</configuration>
